<p style="font-size: 14px; line-height: 1.6; margin-bottom: 16px; text-align: left; color: #ffffff;"><span style="float: left; font-size: 48px; line-height: 0.8; font-weight: bold; padding-right: 8px; padding-top: 4px; color: #ffffff;">D</span>eep in the seas of the world of Estheria, a kingdom of the abyss is said to exist... a kingdom that, for all intents and purposes, makes its threatening air clear. They say none of those who departed to dive into this region of the sea never made it out alive, without a happy end to their tale...</p>
<p style="font-size: 14px; line-height: 1.6; margin-bottom: 16px; text-align: left; color: #ffffff;">...and the reason would probably have to be because of two, very sinister sovereigns that lie inside this said kingdom.</p>
<p style="font-size: 14px; line-height: 1.6; margin-bottom: 16px; text-align: left; color: #ffffff;">Enter <span style="font-size: 1.15em; font-weight: bold;">Lakshmibai</span>, the Terror of Darkwraith. Once having been known as Palisvina, she ruled over the seas with great pride alongside her sister Lurvine, having been two kind souls welcoming lonely treasure hunters that wandered about and sharing stories of aquatic wonders, that had been passed down from generations.</p>
<p style="font-size: 14px; line-height: 1.6; margin-bottom: 16px; text-align: left; color: #ffffff;">They were considered two of Estheria's kindest figures... but once the fated week came and people had started turning on the Sea Sisters, even the Water Goddess herself, the two had been struck with sadness. Sadness which then became guilt, apathy... rage. Consuming powers beyond their own understanding, the Sea Sisters had become two imposingly horrifying figures and sovereigns of the abyss: Nathravina and <span style="font-weight: bold;">Lakshmibai</span>.</p>
<p style="font-size: 14px; line-height: 1.6; margin: 0; text-align: left; color: #ffffff;">Now, any travelers who so much as make the error of traveling too deep down into the sea located in the region of Zethryine are in risk of being engulfed by the Darkwraith...</p>
